  "articleBody": "Finishing out your garage interior turns a dusty utility zone into a clean, durable workshop or functional extension of your home. \n\nKey Benefits: Proper wall and ceiling finishes dramatically improve insulation, reduce dust, upgrade lighting, and protect stored belongings from temperature extremes.\n\nProcess Breakdown: We inspect the slab, exterior walls, and roof structure for moisture leaks. After resolving any damp spots, rough electrical and mechanical work is routed and inspected. High-density insulation goes into studs and rafters, followed by durable drywall, taped and mudded seams, interior painting, and baseboard trim.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start: Decide whether your space will stay a utility garage or become conditioned space. If you're keeping vehicle parking, local building codes mandate specific fire-rated drywall on walls shared with the house, along with sealed penetrations.\n\nTo get clean drywall, solid framing, and quality paint in your garage, call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your finish scope.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}